    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-1450",
      "problem": "For the parabola shown below, find the vertex and the equation of the axis of symmetry.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217628/assets/e88db5363a50530228fefa2e69a9a3a0e1a62eb461103441e61af5c1f7eb6c3b.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The vertex is the \"turning point\" of the parabola. In a downwards parabola, like the one here, the vertex is the maximum point. So, the vertex of this parabola is $(-2,3).$\n\nThe axis of symmetry is the vertical line that passes through the vertex. Therefore, the axis of symmetry of this parabola is $x=-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217628/assets/91e9d323945b1520aa36b70f3faf8c801e28b21437cd1008b54e76dae76d5ccb.png)",
